think Graded every living page of docs-geode at Door -- 29 pages, the first page-by-page reading the shelf has had. All 29 read B+ or better, so no repair was owed and the finding had to come from somewhere the grade cannot reach.
think docs-geode/api/README.md read Status Room seated empty while rishi-language-reference.md had stood in that room since 20260821. Its card read truth_counted=100 composite=95 letter=A -- the highest grade on the shelf, on the page whose first fact was false.
think Two causes, neither the tool erring. Counted Truth resolves the links a page makes and a status line is no link. And at 21 words the page sat under the 8-sentence register floor, so Register and Reach defaulted to 100 and the composite averaged them in; grade_mode=reported says so and the letter does not.
think The index above it was right the whole time: docs-geode/README.md names that room living, because crushed_index_witness reads its table against the rooms on disk every lap. One walled index, thirteen free doors under it, one stale.
think Repairing the api door LOWERED its grade, A/95 reported to A/93 scored -- two points down and the first number that was ever real.
think Censused a second reading nobody holds: a tree path inside a fenced code block, read by neither tracked_link_scan nor counted Truth. Over 438 living pages, 26 unresolved sites, and all 26 correctly absent -- 9 build outputs, 11 reader-created from a tracked .example, 4 written by the shown code, 1 a resolver demo's own input, 1 a glob prefix my pattern truncated.
obs A guard over that class would gate at 26 false positives and zero findings, so I built none and published the reading instead. A refusal with a number attached is worth more than a lantern.
obs The shelf's own front-door claim -- this shelf names none of the pages the doorway guard refuses -- was checked rather than repeated: zero docs-geode refusals across 1,336 pages.
